      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 20 years old woman had an external urethral orifice mass and received an excision operation. Seven years later, she complained a tumor with pain that was similar to the previous tumor. She underwent the tumor removal. Pathological diagnosis was a urethral angiomyomatous leiomyoma in the new concept of estrogen receptor-positive smooth muscle tumors."},
